<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<SharingRules xmlns="http://soap.sforce.com/2006/04/metadata">
    <!--
        RULE 2, Property_Acquisitions_Team_RW, ADDED 2026-08-17. A code review found
        `c/marketDataSync`'s Sync button renders ENABLED for users whose write will be
        refused - `getObjectInfo.updateable` reports object CRUD + FLS only, with no record
        context, so it cannot see sharing. Measured directly on usman-dpeg before writing
        this rule:

          - Property__c OWD is Private (internal AND external).
          - The only pre-existing rule, Property_Acquisition_Queue_RW (below), is an OWNER
            rule sharing records owned by the Acquisition QUEUE. Live Property__c ownership
            was queried directly: ZERO of 48 records are owned by that queue (all 48 are
            owned by two individual users - Usman Khan and Junior Dhanani - because
            LeadConvertService stamps the converting user as owner, never the queue). So the
            pre-existing rule currently matches NOTHING.
          - DPEG_Acquisition_Edit grants Property__c allowEdit=true and viewAllRecords=true
            but modifyAllRecords=false, so a Junior-Analyst-persona user can READ every
            Property but can only EDIT the 1 of 48 they personally own without this rule.

        WHY A CRITERIA RULE, NOT A SECOND OWNER RULE. An owner rule only reaches records
        owned by its sharedFrom population. 47 of the 48 live Property__c records are owned
        by an administrator (Usman Khan) who sits outside every acquisitions role branch, so
        a second owner rule would repeat the existing rule's failure almost exactly. A
        criteria-based rule shares by what the RECORD IS, never by who owns it, which is the
        only construct that reaches all 48 regardless of owner.

        WHY Name notEqual '' AS THE CRITERION. Salesforce criteria rules require at least one
        criteriaItem and reject audit/system fields as ineligible - confirmed on this exact
        object family in Lead.sharingRules-meta.xml's Rule 4 comment ("bad value for
        restricted picklist field: CreatedDate" at deploy), so CreatedDate was not attempted
        here and a real business field was used from the start, following that precedent.
        Property__c.nameField is Text (not auto-number) and is the object's required Name
        field, so it is always populated by construction. Measured directly, not assumed:
        `SELECT COUNT() FROM Property__c` = 48; `SELECT COUNT() FROM Property__c WHERE Name =
        null` = 0. So `Name notEqual ''` matches all 48 of 48 live records.

        WHY DPEG_Acquisitions_Team AND NOT A SECOND PRINCIPALS RULE. Queried GroupMember for
        DPEG_Acquisitions_Team directly: its only two members are the Role group for "DPEG
        Principal" and the RoleAndSubordinatesInternal group for "Acquisitions Analyst" -
        i.e. Nikhil Dhanani (DPEG Principal role) and Junior Dhanani (Acquisitions Analyst
        role, a child role of DPEG Principal) are both already inside this one group by role
        nesting, matching the identical finding recorded in Lead.sharingRules-meta.xml the
        same day. It is also the same population the pre-existing
        Property_Acquisition_Queue_RW rule already targets, so this rule widens WHICH records
        that population can edit, not WHO the population is.

        ACCESS LEVEL IS Edit, AND OBJECT CRUD IS STILL THE CEILING. DPEG_Acquisition_Edit
        (Junior's set) grants allowEdit=true on Property__c; DPEG_Acquisition_View (Nikhil's,
        via DPEG_Principal_PSG) grants allowRead=true / allowEdit=false. Sharing this rule at
        Edit does not over-grant Nikhil - his own object CRUD still caps him to Read. This
        rule DOES grant Edit on every Property__c record to every member of
        DPEG_Acquisitions_Team whose own CRUD allows editing - stated plainly because that is
        the explicit intent, not an incidental side effect.

        🔴 DEPLOY ONE SHARING RULE AT A TIME - established in the 2026-07-22 RBAC build and
        repeated by every sharing-rule file added since (NDA__c, LOI__c, and Lead's Rule 4
        the same day as this one). Deploy this rule alone, separate from any other pending
        sharing-rule change, so a rejection here cannot roll back an unrelated rule and vice
        versa.

        🔴 GROUP MEMBERSHIP IS NOT DEPLOYABLE METADATA and CRITERIA-BASED SHARING
        RECALCULATES ASYNCHRONOUSLY - both standing cautions from the LOI__c/NDA__c/Lead
        files apply identically here. Verify post-deploy via UserRecordAccess for both Junior
        and Nikhil against a broad sample of Property__c records, not just the ones used to
        author this rule, and do not expect access to appear instantly.

        Do NOT remove or modify Property_Acquisition_Queue_RW below - it is dormant today
        (matches zero records) but is the correct rule for queue-owned Property__c records,
        and retiring it is a separate, evidenced decision this change does not make.
    -->
    <sharingOwnerRules>
        <fullName>Property_Acquisition_Queue_RW</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Edit</accessLevel>
        <label>Property Acquisition Queue RW</label>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>DPEG_Acquisitions_Team</group>
        </sharedTo>
        <sharedFrom>
            <queue>Acquisition</queue>
        </sharedFrom>
    </sharingOwnerRules>
    <sharingCriteriaRules>
        <fullName>Property_Acquisitions_Team_RW</fullName>
        <accessLevel>Edit</accessLevel>
        <description>Business requirement: every Property__c record must be editable by the acquisitions team (DPEG_Acquisitions_Team), regardless of owner. Name is used as an always-true criterion (Property__c.nameField is Text, is required, and measured 0 of 48 live records with a blank Name) because owner-based sharing cannot reach the administrator who owns 47 of the 48 live records, and the pre-existing Property_Acquisition_Queue_RW rule below matches zero records since no Property__c is owned by the Acquisition queue. See the in-root comment at the top of this file for the full measurement.</description>
        <label>Property Acquisitions Team RW</label>
        <criteriaItems>
            <field>Name</field>
            <operation>notEqual</operation>
            <value></value>
        </criteriaItems>
        <sharedTo>
            <group>DPEG_Acquisitions_Team</group>
        </sharedTo>
    </sharingCriteriaRules>
</SharingRules>

